bibtex2xml applies to downloaded html files bibtex format from MathSciNet
(test.xml)

then: dress the full xml file
(data.xml)

run PreProcess.xsl on data.xml output to MathSci.xml

run: 

perl DBMaker.pl MathSci year author journal author


All of the above is done by the shell script: 

>>>> MakeDB <<<<

*******************************************************************

Potential problems: 

look for author line that is split. put all on one line.

*******************************************************************


TO RUN:

java DATABASE.Data portnum MathSci.properties

FROM THE BROWSER:

Start at MathSci.searchpage.html ... 

########
NOTE: You do not need to restart the server when remaking the database nor #######
when reconfiguring the output style file `runit.xsl'                       #######
